// A block-form `sub` (`sub P = e { ... }`, spec §4.5) whose BLOCK contains a
// call-induced draw of the atom it binds. The block is where the binding is
// LIVE, so the draw is covered and the program is accepted and runs.
//
// This is the regression guard for the checker fix that made a `sub`'s
// provision its own lexical scope: an interim version excluded the block
// (`Sub.c`) as if it were the initializer and wrongly refused this with
// EXS-E0421, though the lowering accepted it. The checker is the authority
// for the capability rule (CLAUDE.md), so it must accept exactly what the
// lowering accepts -- this file is the "accepts" half, byte for byte through
// the whole pipeline.
//
// `getenv` draws `ambitus`; `initium` holds it only through the `sub`, which
// binds it for the block. `use(getenv())` draws inside the block -> covered.
// `ambitus` (not `archivum`) so the binary's closure stays within the audit's
// default {Mundus, ambitus} -- the atom is immaterial to the lexical-scope
// rule under test. Exit 0 (the block's `redde` returns `use`'s 0).

functio getenv() -> ambitus poscit ambitus { redde ambitus; }

functio use(a: ambitus) -> u8 { redde 0; }

publica functio initium(m: Mundus) -> u8 {
    firma a = m.ambitus();
    sub ambitus = a {
        firma k = use(getenv());
        redde k;
    }
    redde 0;
}
